# Root .dockerignore
#
# The `orchestrator` / `orchestrator-test` and `slack-gateway` /
# `slack-gateway-test` Compose services build from the repository root
# (each Dockerfile COPYs packages/agent-contracts plus its own service
# directory explicitly). The remaining services (hermes-agent,
# google-calendar-mcp) build from their own subdirectory context and are
# unaffected by this file.
#
# Every pattern below uses a **/ prefix, except .git/ (inherently root-only
# -- this repo has no submodules). Unlike .gitignore, a bare `name` or
# `name/` pattern in .dockerignore matches ONLY at the context root, not at
# any depth -- confirmed empirically, including against a real case in this
# repo: packages/approvals/.venv sits one level below root, and a bare
# `.venv/` pattern does not exclude it from the build context.

# Git metadata
.git/

# Environment variables
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Secrets and credentials
**/credentials.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/token.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Python virtual environments
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Python bytecode, build output, and package caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/

# Test caches and coverage artifacts
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage.xml

# Node.js
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Local databases and application data
**/data/
**/memory/
**/postgres-data/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Ollama models
**/models/
**/ollama-data/

# Logs and traces
**/logs/
**/traces/
**/exports/

# Editor / IDE / OS artifacts
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Claude Code local session state
**/.claude/
